msgid ""
"While pgRouting functions provide a low-level interface, developing for a"
" higher-level application requires these requirements to be represented "
"directly in the SQL queries. As these SQL queries get more complex, it is"
" desirable to store them in PostgreSQL stored procedures or functions. "
"Stored procedures or functions are an effective way to wrap application "
"logic, in this case, related to routing logic and requirements."
msgstr ""

